<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43610" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔδειπν-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with goodly feasts</i>,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαῖτες εὔ</span>.
				<i>well-appointed, sumptuous</i> feasts, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Med.</u>
				200
			</span></i> (anap.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			epith. of departed souls to whom offerings were made (cf. foreg.), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρ᾽ εὐδείπνοις ἔσῃ ἄτιμος
					ἐμπύροισι κνισωτοῖς χθονός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					484
				</span></i>
			; taken by some Gramm. as applied to the festival itself, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">Phot.,
					<u>EM</u>42.3</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
